  "notes": "One entry per report of tests/fixtures/reports/{cobertura,opencover,lcov,jacoco,clover}. `parser` holds the totals of the parsers, which follow Codecov; `oracle` those of ReportGenerator, read with its own parsers. `differences` lists every line where the two disagree, on the state or on the branches (`covered/total`); an empty list means they agree on every line. A difference is never fixed in the parser to please the oracle: each one names a rule of `rules`, which says what each tool does and why the parser follows Codecov. Paths are compared without their prefix: a path is not a coverage difference, PathFixer resolves it later.",
  "rules": {
    "lcov-branches-ignored-in-js": {
      "codecov": "services/report/languages/lcov.py, lines 87 and 146: a file whose name ends with `.js` drops its `BRDA` entries (and `FN`), so the line keeps its `DA` hits and has no branch data.",
      "reportGenerator": "Parser/LCovParser.cs (v5.5.12), lines 149 and 226-231: `BRDA` is read for every file, and an executed line with a branch never taken is `PartiallyCovered`.",
      "parserFollows": "Codecov, see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §6.3.",
      "configurable": false
    },
    "jacoco-partial-from-branches": {
      "codecov": "services/report/languages/jacoco.py, lines 115-117: a line with `mb` > 0 is the branch `cb/(mb+cb)`, so one missed branch out of two is a partial, whatever the instructions say.",
      "reportGenerator": "Parser/JaCoCoParser.cs (v5.5.12), lines 212-214: the status of a line only reads the instructions, `partiallyCovered` being `mi` > 0. A line with `mi=0` and a missed branch is `Covered`; its branches are kept apart, here `1/2`.",
      "parserFollows": "Codecov, see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §6.3.",
      "configurable": false
    },
    "clover-cond-is-a-line": {
      "codecov": "services/report/languages/clover.py, lines 84-92: a `type=\"cond\"` line is a coverable branch line, `0/2`, `1/2` or `2/2`.",
      "reportGenerator": "Parser/CloverParser.cs (v5.5.12), line 150: only `type=\"stmt\"` lines are coverable; a `cond` only gives branch data to a `stmt` of the same number. Istanbul writes `cond` instead of `stmt`, so these lines do not exist for ReportGenerator.",
      "parserFollows": "Codecov, see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §6.3.",
      "configurable": false
    }
  },
